-- title:
--   Eichler–Shimura compatibility for the Hecke–diamond ring of J₁(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$. Write $J_1(M)$ for [`ModularCurve.JOne M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186), the degree-zero divisor class group over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the base-changed $q$-expansion function field $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot\mathbb Q(X_1(M))$, and let $\mathrm{heckeDiamondGenBar}\ M$ be the family of $\mathbb Z$-linear endomorphisms of $J_1(M)$ indexed by $\mathrm{Primes}\sqcup\mathbb N$ given on $\ell$ by `heckeOperatorOneBar M ℓ` (the $\mathbb Z$-linear map underlying `heckeOperatorOneAlong (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) M ℓ`) and on $d$ by `diamondOneBar M d` (the action on $J_1(M)$ of the diamond automorphism `diamondAutBar M d` viewed as a semilinear automorphism). Assume `HeckeDiamondInputsAll M`: the predicate `HeckeInputsOneAlong (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) M ℓ` holds for every prime $\ell$, and for every $d$ coprime to $M$ there exist an automorphism of `x1FunctionField M` over $\mathbb Q$ satisfying `IsDiamondAut M d` and an automorphism of `x1FunctionFieldBar M` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which is a base change of `diamondAut M d`. Assume `HeckeDiamondCommuteBar M`: these generators commute pairwise. Then there is a ring homomorphism $\Phi$ from the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb Z}(J_1(M))$ generated by all of them to $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}(S_2(\Gamma_1(M)))$ such that: $\Phi$ is injective; for every prime $\ell\nmid M$, $\Phi$ sends `heckeOperatorOneBar M ℓ` to [`CuspForm.heckeTLinOne 2`](def/CuspForm_Gamma1HeckeOperators.html#L652), namely $f\mapsto \sum_{j<\ell} f\mid_2\begin{pmatrix}1&j\\0&\ell\end{pmatrix}+(\langle\ell\rangle f)\mid_2\begin{pmatrix}\ell&0\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$; for every $d$ coprime to $M$, $\Phi$ sends `diamondOneBar M d` to [`CuspForm.diamondLinOne M 2 d`](def/CuspForm_Gamma1HeckeOperators.html#L592), the slash action of a matrix in $\Gamma_0(M)$ with lower-right entry $\equiv d \pmod M$ (the identity if no such lift exists); and for every prime $\ell\mid M$, every $f\in S_2(\Gamma_1(M))$ and every $n\in\mathbb N$, the $n$-th coefficient of the width-one $q$-expansion of $\Phi($`heckeOperatorOneBar M ℓ`$)f$ equals the $\ell n$-th coefficient of that of $f$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura compatibility between the divisorial Hecke and diamond correspondences on the Jacobian of $X_1(M)$ and the Hecke operators on weight-two cusp forms, stated simultaneously for all generators: beyond pinning $T_\ell$ for $\ell\nmid M$ and the diamonds, the last clause identifies the operator attached to $\ell\mid M$ as $U_\ell$ through its effect on $q$-expansions. It is used in the study of primitive forms to transfer Hecke eigenvalues, including $U_\ell$-eigenvalues at primes dividing the level, between cusp forms and the Tate modules of $J_1(M)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_injective_ringHom_adjoin_heckeDiamondGenBar_cuspForm_qCoeff.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_Gamma1HeckeOperators

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

theorem ModularCurve.exists_injective_ringHom_adjoin_heckeDiamondGenBar_cuspForm_qCoeff
    (M : ℕ) [NeZero M]
    (hin : ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsAll M) (hcomm : ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondCommuteBar M) :
    ∃ Φ : ↥(Algebra.adjoin ℤ (Set.range (ModularCurve.heckeDiamondGenBar M))) →+*
        Module.End ℂ (CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma1 M) 2),
      Function.Injective Φ ∧
      (∀ (ℓ : Nat.Primes) (hℓM : ¬ (ℓ : ℕ) ∣ M),
        Φ ⟨ModularCurve.heckeOperatorOneBar M ℓ,
            Algebra.subset_adjoin (Set.mem_range_self (Sum.inl ℓ))⟩
          = CuspForm.heckeTLinOne 2 ℓ.prop hℓM) ∧
      (∀ (d : ℕ), Nat.Coprime d M →
        Φ ⟨ModularCurve.diamondOneBar M d,
            Algebra.subset_adjoin (Set.mem_range_self (Sum.inr d))⟩
          = CuspForm.diamondLinOne M 2 d) ∧
      ∀ (ℓ : Nat.Primes), (ℓ : ℕ) ∣ M →
        ∀ (f : CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma1 M) 2) (n : ℕ),
          ModularFormClass.qCoeff
              (Φ ⟨ModularCurve.heckeOperatorOneBar M ℓ,
                  Algebra.subset_adjoin (Set.mem_range_self (Sum.inl ℓ))⟩ f) n
            = ModularFormClass.qCoeff f (ℓ * n) := by sorry
